sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Kavanagh et al. (2013) phalangeal Inhibitory Cascade & Hiscock et al. (2017) BMP-GDF5-Noggin synovial joint interzone segmentation, with Pass 3 reduced Biot poroelastic synovial cavitation — MorphoEval overall 89.4/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) re-scored evaluation of `2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py` (overall weighted score 89.4/100, down 7.2 from the v2 score of 96.6). The single v2 remediation item is closed: the 2D Gdf5 interzone field now drives a reduced Biot poroelastic cavitation solver (hyaluronan synthesis, Donnan osmotic pore pressure with Darcy drainage, HA/CD44 loss of cohesion, irreversible cavity phase field, Carter-Wong articular arch, Kahn Sox9 reversion) that reproduces the three literature outcomes (motile WT 3 interzones -> 3 cavities; paralysed 3 -> 0 with interzone Sox9 0.81 vs 0.23; Nog-/- 0 -> 0), has monotone muscle-loading (m* = 0.80) and permeability sweeps, matches the radiograph joint-line sagitta/chord (0.064 vs 0.056 +/- 0.078; 3/4 joints convex-head sign), and is backed by two new machine-verified Lean 4 theorems (5 total, 0 sorrys). Scoring the current file line by line, however, exposed defects that v2 did not deduct for: templated joint positions and hard-coded PIP fusion in the RD PDE, an imposed rather than emergent articular arch (the modelled head contour is flat), a juvenile specimen with a low-contrast Digit II centerline and a hard-coded cleft count, and several uncited Pass 3 calibration constants. These are carried as 8 line-pinned Pass 4 items. Overall 89.4/100 (faithfulness 87.1, reproducibility 94.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 93, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 96, Code-to-model traceability 92, Reproducibility package 95. Output judged: docs/media/joint_interzone_clefting_comparison.png: rendered output of 2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py at d58a084, image/png, 1021079 B, 2610×1566 px, artifact_sha256 470eccc646ae90364db947ce1ca8c2b1c26eaf3376459c24b222180df47cd5c5 (sha256 470eccc646ae90364db947ce1ca8c2b1c26eaf3376459c24b222180df47cd5c5), spec_fingerprint 1d288d48a8d6a46b269ac8c181dfcb21e621b3dfef13912fa8b3a56d847f9a0e. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 1d288d48a8d6a46b269ac8c181dfcb21e621b3dfef13912fa8b3a56d847f9a0e; artifact_sha256: 470eccc646ae90364db947ce1ca8c2b1c26eaf3376459c24b222180df47cd5c5; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/joint_interzone_clefting/joint_interzone_clefting_reference.json=8ce3cc464602a827..., datasets/joint_interzone_clefting/paper_citations.bib=4dba5970a1ffae76..., datasets/joint_interzone_clefting/scout_manifest.json=1ae24e293d2062b2..., datasets/joint_interzone_clefting/synovial_cavitation_reference.json=9ca273ead3e3606e..., datasets/joint_interzone_clefting/tetrapod_digit_interzone_specimen.jpg=995e43a2a0cf7815...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-joint-interzone-clefting-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Kavanagh et al. (2013): phalanx lengths of triphalangeal digits across tetrapods fall on the inhibitory-cascade line P2/P1 = 1/2 + 1/2 (P3/P1), i.e. P2 is 1/3 of the phalangeal total | Hiscock et al. (2017), Hartmann & Tabin (2001): periodic Gdf5+/Wnt9a+ interzones segment a chondrogenic digit ray; Brunet et al. (1998): Nog-/- embryos form no joints; Storm et al. (1994): Gdf5 bp/bp fuses interphalangeal joints | Drachman & Sokoloff (1966), Kahn et al. (2009): paralysed or muscle-less embryos specify interzones but fail to cavitate and the interzone re-chondrifies; Roddy et al. (2011): immobilised rudiments lose articular curvature | Edwards et al. (1994), Dowthwaite et al. (1998): cavitation coincides with mechanosensitive hyaluronan accumulation and loss of interzone cohesion; Mow et al. (1980), Maroudas (1976): cartilage is a biphasic poroelastic solid whose Donnan swelling pressure is ~0.1-0.25 MPa; reconstructed_in_script: GDF5-Noggin 2x2 Turing dispersion with D=0 control; 1D growing-domain RD PDE with a distal PFR mask; 2D digit-ray view; Kavanagh 12-taxon morphospace regression; six genetic/signalling perturbations; radiograph segmentation of Digits II-IV | Pass 3: reduced 2D Biot storage-equation cavitation solver (HA synthesis -> osmotic pore pressure with free drainage -> cohesion threshold -> irreversible cavity phase field), three literature cavitation conditions, muscle-loading and permeability sweeps, Carter-Wong articular arch, Kahn Sox9 reversion, and the radiograph joint-line sagitta/chord comparison; transfer_boundary: The 1D RD PDE does not self-organise its joint positions: `joint_targets` are pre-computed from the arithmetic progression and injected as a Gaussian source behind the PFR, and the bp/bp PIP fusion is hard-coded (L334-349, L364-373); the Turing dispersion is verified analytically, not as the pattern-selecting mechanism of the PDE | The poroelastic solver has a rigid solid skeleton (no u-p Biot displacement, effective stress, capsule or ligament), is 2D, one-way coupled (RD -> poroelastic), and its articular arch is a parametric Carter-Wong rule a(y) = A_arc phi(m)(1 - (y/W)^2), not a computed growth response; all constants are dimensionless and scaled only to adult cartilage | The vendored specimen is a juvenile hand radiograph with open physes, not an embryonic interzone section; the joint-line arch statistic rests on 4 valid joints with sd > mean; does_not_claim: A full Biot u-p or triphasic solution, 3D geometry, synovial fluid flow, capsule/ligament mechanics, convex-head emergence from growth (the model's head contour is flat because the lens cancels the arch), or any dimensional embryonic poroelastic constant." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: 2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py:1019-1023 and 1053 — Digit II's stored centerline has no bone contrast over its distal half (profile ~67 flat), so its DIP minimum is set by the window fraction, and `n_synovial_clefts: 3` is a constant. Re-trace the Digit II centerline through bone, detect the cleft count from the number of radiolucent minima with a contrast gate, and separate the joint space from the physis minimum 10-12 px distal (the specimen is juvenile).",
            "remediation needed: 2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py:1598-1619 — the Sox9 reversion ratio and the loading threshold m* carry `reference_value: null`. Replace with a quantitative anchor (e.g. Kahn 2009 Fig. 4 Col2a1 signal in the muscle-less interzone, or Roddy 2011's graded immobilisation series) or move them out of the validation set into a 'predictions' list.",
            "remediation needed: 2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py:1872-1879 vs 1882 — `--m-load` / `--permeability` only reach `render_cavitation_figure`; Panel C of the comparison figure always uses m_load = 1 and 0. Thread the CLI values through `render_comparison_figure` and add a requirements lock file for the slot.",
            "remediation needed: 2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py:334-349 and 364-373 — the 1D RD PDE places its interzones at pre-computed `joint_targets` injected as Gaussian `wave_drive` sources and hard-codes the Gdf5 bp/bp PIP fusion with `if cleft_amp < 0.35 and idx_j == 1: continue`. Replace the template with genuine wavelength selection (PFR-modulated D_G, D_N or kinetic parameters so the Turing wavelength of Law 2 sets the phalanx lengths) and let the bp/bp fusion follow from a Gdf5-dose-dependent cohesion/threshold.",
            "remediation needed: 2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py:566-591 and 666 — A_arc_over_W = 0.22, K_identity = 0.30, kappa_G = 0.5, r_cav = 3.0 and the Kahn reversion factor 0.85 are uncited calibrations. Sweep A_arc and kappa_G (parameter-expressivity), and anchor at least kappa_G / sigma_0 to the Edwards 1994 / Maroudas 1976 ratio of interzone cohesion to Donnan pressure, or state them as free in the docstring and reference JSON.",
            "remediation needed: 2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py:566-663 — the poroelastic solver is a storage equation with a rigid skeleton; add the solid displacement u and effective stress (Biot u-p, or at least a 1D consolidation column across the interzone) so that the tissue separation and the articular arch arise from strain, not from the parametric rule at L631-633.",
            "remediation needed: 2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py:631-640 and 691-751 — the modelled proximal head contour is flat (head sagitta/half-span -0.036) because the Darcy lens thickens at the midline and cancels the imposed arch; the radiograph heads are convex. Either let the cavity reach the capsule periphery (Robin instead of Dirichlet drainage at the perichondrium) or compute the arch from a Carter-Wong growth law so a convex head / concave base pair emerges, and assert head_sagitta_norm > 0 in self-test check 12.",
            "remediation needed: 2016-onuff-joint-interzone-clefting.py:869-948 — the joint-line arch statistic rests on 4 valid joints with sd 0.078 > mean 0.056. Add a second radiograph (adult, closed physes) or trace the MCP joints as well, and report a bootstrap CI so the model-specimen comparison in check 12 is not a 0.05 tolerance." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.894"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Claude Fable 5.1 (MorphoEval Autonomous Loop Slot 018 Pass 3 Assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "claude-fable-5-1" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://www.anthropic.com> .
}

